WPE WebKit 2.52.4 — softfp JIT enablement for the HP TouchPad (Atlas browser)

Cortex-A8 / softfp / Thumb2 target (webOS 3.0.5 system libs are softfp). Three changes:

1. JavaScriptCore/jit/CCallHelpers.h — restore soft-float FP-call ABI marshalling (ported from
   WebKit 2.34.6). Modern WebKit hardcodes the hardfp convention (doubles in d0/d1); on our softfp
   build the C operations (fmod/floor/ceil/round/...) read GP register pairs, so JIT-emitted calls
   returned garbage. Passes double args in even-aligned GP register pairs and reads double returns
   from r0:r1. Guarded #if CPU(ARM_THUMB2) && !CPU(ARM_HARDFP) so hardfp builds are unaffected.
   This is what makes DFG correct (modulo/Math were wrong before).

2. JavaScriptCore/assembler/CPU.h — relax the prologueStackPointerDelta #error guard.
3. WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h — JIT/DFG enablement gates.

Apply from the WebKit source root with: patch -p1 < wpewebkit-2.52.4-softfp-jit.patch

--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/CCallHelpers.h
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/CCallHelpers.h
